1
00:00:00,860 --> 00:00:04,040
This is the whole history
of the Earth on one line:

2
00:00:04,090 --> 00:00:08,590
four and a half billion years, from its
formation on the left to today on the

3
00:00:08,640 --> 00:00:14,230
right. The bands are the four eons. Almost
everything you'd find in a museum is

4
00:00:14,280 --> 00:00:17,434
crammed into that last
sliver at the right.

5
00:00:19,104 --> 00:00:23,064
The Earth forms about four
and a half billion years ago.

6
00:00:23,114 --> 00:00:25,944
About a billion years later there's life:

7
00:00:25,994 --> 00:00:30,024
microbial mats that left
stromatolites behind.

8
00:00:30,074 --> 00:00:35,314
Around two point four billion years ago,
their oxygen starts to fill the air.

9
00:00:35,364 --> 00:00:38,860
For about three billion
years, that's what life is.

10
00:00:40,290 --> 00:00:45,170
Zoom into that sliver and it
opens up. The Cambrian explosion,

11
00:00:45,220 --> 00:00:48,520
five hundred and thirty-nine
million years ago.

12
00:00:48,570 --> 00:00:52,590
Plants on land. A fish
walking out of the water.

13
00:00:52,640 --> 00:00:56,050
The Great Dying, the worst
extinction we know of.

14
00:00:56,100 --> 00:01:00,680
The first dinosaurs. And
sixty-six million years ago,

15
00:01:00,730 --> 00:01:01,963
the asteroid.

16
00:01:03,443 --> 00:01:09,433
Keep going. The last seven million
years: the earliest members of the human

17
00:01:09,483 --> 00:01:14,513
lineage. Our own species appears only
about three hundred thousand years ago,

18
00:01:14,563 --> 00:01:16,108
right at the edge.

19
00:01:17,578 --> 00:01:21,138
And the last twelve thousand
years: farming, then writing,

20
00:01:21,188 --> 00:01:26,118
then the pyramids. All of recorded history
fits in a space you couldn't see at

21
00:01:26,168 --> 00:01:27,964
all when we started.

22
00:01:29,444 --> 00:01:33,424
And still it goes: down to the
second the Eagle landed on the Moon,

23
00:01:33,474 --> 00:01:36,294
on the same line where
the Earth was formed.

24
00:01:36,344 --> 00:01:39,084
Change how the line is
read, and nothing moves:

25
00:01:39,134 --> 00:01:43,344
every time is stored exactly.
From eons to seconds,

26
00:01:43,394 --> 00:01:45,754
it's one timeline.
